Hello,

The new and updated KDE version 2.1.1 is now available for download, as
usual for all major Linux distributions as well as for Compaq Tru64 Unix.
Even though this version is a bug-fix release only, there is one Tru64
specific enhancement: SSL web sites can now be opened with the Konqueror
web browser. This was made possible with the help of the Konqueror SSL
developer George Staikos and by including the PRNGD entropy gathering
daemon in the distribution. The necessary source-code parts were back-
ported from the KDE 2.2 source tree.

Tru64 Unix specific fixes include:

- packaging fixes for libz.so problem with lnusertemp
- included the missing libXpm.so file.
- included PRNGD which is started automatically when the first KDE
  user logs in. So PRNGD does not run as root and it's completely
  transparent to the users. Also an already existing PRNGD or EGD daemon
  can be used as well.
- printing in konqueror works now.

For non-Tru64 specific fixes and changes, please see the official KDE
2.1.1 announcement on www.kde.org. It should should show up today or in
the next days on:

          http://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-2.1.1.html

KOFFICE is again included in this release. Please note, however, that this
software has alpha-version status and is only included to get an impres-
sion of what KOffice will look like when it's finished. It is expected to
be ready in about half a year (late 2001). First betas will be released
independently of KDE2 and will appear at the end of May.

KDE 2.1.1 for Tru64 Unix can be downloaded from:

          ftp://ftp.radar.tugraz.at/pub/kde2/tru64/2.1.1

More informations are on:

          ftp://ftp.radar.tugraz.at/pub/kde2/tru64/2.1.1/README.Tru64

Thanks to the KDE development team for their hard and good work and for
supporting me to make this possible.

Future developments: The first beta of KDE 2.2 is scheduled to be released
mid April 2001. There's no final release date yet. Some of the improve-
ments we'll see in KDE 2.2 is a better printing environment as well as
IMAP support for KMail. I will include OpenGL support in my Tru64 Port
based on the Mesa OpenGL libraries, to get the remaining GL screensavers
working.

Dr. Tom Leitner, tom@radar.tu-graz.ac.at, Mar. 26th, 2001
