You need to dbx the kernel and set the ICMP rejectmask accordingly:

# dbx -k /vmunix
(dbx) assign icmp_rejectcodemask=0x20
32

You can do this for other ICMP types by setting the bit corresponding
to the types defined in ip_icmp.h (ICMP_REDIRECT is bit 5).  To make
this permanent accross a reboot, you can use the "patch" command in
dbx, or you can put the assignment in a startup script like /etc/inet.local
that gets run at boot time.

BTW, check into why you're getting the redirect, that router might be
trying to tell you something.

-Brian
