farul ghazali wrote:

> System is an ES40 pedestal running Tru64 5.0A with three channel PCI
> SWXCR controller (KZPAC?) connected to the internal disk arrays. The
> problem I'm having is that swxcrmgr from within the OS is complaining
> that it can't find any xcr controllers.
>
> The ARC console version of swxcrmgr works fine, I've setup the disks
> that way. What do I need to use swxcrmgr from within the OS while the
> system is up?
>
> TIA

This utility does not look at the new Tru64 device naming conventions.
In my case, it was looking for a file called /dev/rre0c, as that is the
'c' slice
on  disk 0 of my 3 channel array.  So - what I did was create a link to
/devices/rdisk/dsk0c and called it /dev/rre0c. That worked for me - you
may need to change the 0 to something else if your raid array is not
disk0.

I used the command :
ln -s /devices/rdisk/dsk0c /dev/rre0c.
Hope this helps....let me know if you have other problems...




