Mike Mohr wrote:
> 
> First of all, hp3_lptr is not a valid name.  The correct syntax (per RFC822) is
> {{letter|digit}{0{letter|digit|hyphen}...n{letter|digit|hyphen}}}.
> 
> In other words, hp3-lptr is correct, hp3_lptr is not.  If your DNS contains the
> underscore, have your networks people fix the problem as soon as possible.
> The Compaq/Digital is a little more intollerant of errors than HP.
> 

I strongly second that! Depending on the version of BIND (8, I think),
chances are high that suddenly your DNS doesn't work at all or only in
degraded performance, because the primary DNS server simply refuses to
load a zone containing A records with '_', and the secondary refuses to
refresh his zone. Normally, you'll find a notice about this in the
primary DNS server's log files.

This happenend here once, and because unfortunately the syslogd wasn't
running anymore on that server we could not see any message in the logs.
It took me 4 hours to finally figure out what has happened....

