I think it depends on which version of ARC you have.  In the most recent 
version I have used, one of the menus off the main screen has an 
"advanced" option (look at the bottom of the screen to see which 
function key to press to enter "advanced" mode) where you can change 
this.  I recall reading that in earlier versions of ARC this was set 
from a "boot" option on the main ARC menu.

> Maybe I should set jumper 31 (i think it is), boot up into the ARC, and
> select "firmware update" and throw in the "firmware update v5.8" ?

I think you would simply end up with both SRM and ARC installed.  You 
would still need to change the setting that takes the machine into ARC 
at boot time.

> Second:
> When I have switched to SRM and updated the BIOS, are there any gotcha's
> when I install Tru64? The installation guide gives the impression that I
> basically don't have to anything special (they always do), but I would
