For the Tru64 V5.1 release, running spike on the kernel can only
be done with a patched linker.  I know that patched linker is
available in patchkit 2.  (It might even be in patchkit 1).

However, with the patchkit linker, there is one more step that
must be done before running spike on the kernel.   Before building
the kernel with the doconfig utility, you need to set the 
 __ENABLE_KERNEL_SPIKING environment variable.

In summary:
	- Get the patched linker.
	- Set the __ENABLE_KERNEL_SPIKING environment variable.
	- Run doconfig to create a new kernel.
	- Run spike on the new kernel.

Running spike on kernels prior to the V5.1 release is not supported.
The above environment variable workaround is only needed for the
V5.1 release.  Releases that will ship after V5.1 will not use it.

Joe Mario
Compaq Tru64 UNIX Development Environment.


