Forgive me for asking a rather lame question that certainly is
answered in manuals or elsewhere, but I suppose there's a really quick
answer to this:

On IRIX and for instance Redhat Linux you may modify the symbolic
links in the rc-runlevel directories with a command called
chkconfig. For instance, you may say 'chkconfig sendmail off', which
will prevent sendmail from being started when entering runlevel 3, 4
or 5. You may also list all services and what runlevels they are
started in by giving a --list parameter.

Similarly, at least on Redhat there is a simple command-line interface
to start/stop/restart/poll status of processes started by init through
the rc-runlevel scripts called 'service', example usage 'service httpd
start'.

Are there any equivalents to these commands in Tru64? I did check some
of the manuals on the www.tru64unix.compaq.com site, but what I found
was either graphical interfaces or otherwise not what I looked for.

Regards


-- 
Audun Nordal


