Hi,

the dynamic routes are created through an server/router which has
the option set to send ICMP redirect messages. This can be turned off.

Your system wants to send a packet along a "wrong" route. This
router catches the paket and sends it to the "right" adress and sends
your system this redirect messages.

you can avoid this by turning this feature off of the router.
im not sure with TRU64 but at least with linux it is possible to discard all
incoming
redirect messages because this feature can be exploited.

also see "tcp/ip illustrated volume 1" chapter 9 from W. Richard Stevens

have fun
SaKe

