First, what shell are you using ? sh ?  ksh ?  csh ?
If your using csh you must use the syntax
	limit datasize  ######

Second, what are your hard limits set to ? 
	ulimit -h    (sh)
	ulimit -Ha   (ksh)
	limit -h     (csh)

I don't believe it is not possible for even root to exceed a hard limit.

If the hard limit is too low for your satisfaction, you need to run
dxkerneltuner (as root) and select the proc section and change either
(both ?)  max-per-proc-address-space or per-proc-address-space.

RTFM  System Configuration and Tuning


Jack


