X  How can i set quota on directory in a Trucluster 5.1 environment ?

I do not think you can (at least not directly).

You could use AdvFS and create a fileset, establish a fileset quota
(man chfsets), then mount the fileset on the directory.  This should
work.  And since an AdvFS domain can have multiple filesets, you could
create one fileset with its own individual fileset quota for each
subdirectory tree you need to have quotas associated with.

NOTE:  Fileset quotas work even in a cluster.  I think that 
       user and group quotas for cluster file systems 
       will be coming soon.

                                Bob Harris

