Note that you are comparing the C++ compiler to the C compiler.

The C compiler has never supported a "-std gnu" switch, the C++
compiler added it in V6.3 and later. You can read the cxx man
page to see what is supported under that switch.

It has been a goal to support some common gcc extenstions in
Compaq C in the -std (default, relaxed ANSI) mode, so the use
of a "-std gnu" switch should not be necessary.

If you find a common, useful "gcc-ism" in the code that you
think should be supported by Compaq C, let us know.

Thanks,
-Jeff


