In article <3AA23004.B3B87250@vie.ce.philips.com>, "R. Schicht" <schicht@vie.ce.philips.com> writes:
>
>As i am new to True64 (i come from Solaris)  i have the task to monitor
>the general disc I/O and the I/O of specific devices (4.0,5.0 on Alpha
>4x00).
>
>What commands are there to do so (or what OS-tools)?

The command included in the base system on all versions is
iostat(1).  Left to itself it only reports I/O statistics
(request rate and data rate) on the first four disks, but
the manual page will explain how to get it to print data
on more disks.

>
>Are there some useful tools to download anywhere (where?)?

The Open Source CDROM and Freeware CDROM should have other
utilities on it.  Monitor can display the disk data as well
as other system summary information and save it to a file
for later reply.  The version on the V4 Freeware CDROM is
suitable for V4 and earlier.  For V5 you'll need to get the
version on:

	ftp.digital.com:/pub/DEC/monitor.alpha.tar.Z

This also compiles and runs all the way back to DEC OSF/1 V1.3.

On some systems, the V4 version on the Freeware CDROM can't
collect some of the disk data and generates a core file in
the process.  The version on ftp.digital.com fixes this.  If
your system has the problem, send me mail and I'll try to
remember the Makefile change that fixes it.

All available is Collect.  It gets pretty much the same data
as Monitor, but lends itself to much better report generation.
I don't know how it does for live monitoring.

