before bugging you guys with them.  Need your help if I'm
going to keep some vestiges of my hair.

We have:
Alpha 4100 Tru64 v4.0F running for 4 years now.
ES40 Tru64 v5.0 coming up.
Both are running C2 security for password purposes, not
other stuff.

1. Problem on both systems: Server daemons for client-server
application and 'at' jobs create files with -rw------
permissions.
This is a problem for us because
a) One must to be root in order to view user created files.
Our policy is to restrict root access to only a couple of
people.  Application manager needs to view user files to
debug application problems.
b) Application runs 'at' processes for batch reports, then
tries to delete the files but can't.
I've done a kludge to work around (b), but not (a).
c) 'at' jobs in general create files that noone but user can
read.
Compaq support said only solution is to patch the kernal.
I have a hard time with that.

2. Problem on ES40 v5.0 system, but not 4100 v4.0F
We do much support via telnet.   We do not allow root login
via telnet, just from the console.  On the new ES40 v5.0
system we can su to root, but from there an 'su username'
and 'su - username' command requires a password.
This is a problem for us because:
a)  Problem for debugging user problems because sometimes we
must ask them to tell us their password, which creates bad
habits.
b)  Problem when needing to run scripts which include 'su
oracle -c commands'.
On the 4100 v4.0F we can telnet in, 'su root', then 'su
user' or 'su - user' without a password, but not on the ES40
v5.0 system.

