"system" <wongpk@tuteee.starhub.net.sg> wrote in message news:3aa44e9d@news.starhub.net.sg...
> Hi there is there a way I can see what RAID my system is running running?

Start with the output from sys_check and the system boot logs.
This should tell you which controllers are managing your RAID.
If you have swxcr(mylex) controllers then use the swxcrmgr software to
interrogate them.
If you have HZx Controllers then use hsxterm to interrogate them (connect
to the command console lun). Or you can connect a serial cable to the
console connection on the controller and interrogate it that way.
This should be enough to get you started.
Adam





