Hello,

There's a problem installing KDE 2.1 under Tru64 5.1 running in enhanced
security mode. The original install_kde script only checked for Tru64
version 5.0 when modifying certain file permissions. This leads to the
situation that under 5.1 running enhanced security, the kcheckpass program
is installed with improper permissions and once the screensaver comes up,
the password is never recognized.

A manual fix for this is to enter this as root:

     chown root:auth /usr/local/kde21/bin/kcheckpass
     chmod 4755 /usr/local/kde21/bin/kcheckpass

An updated install_kde script for new installations is available here:

     ftp://ftp.radar.tugraz.at/pub/kde2/tru64/2.1/install_kde

Additionally I have made all files available via HTTP now as well,
for people behind an http-only proxy. The URL is:

     http://ftp.radar.tugraz.at/kde/

Tom
