I recently decided to upgrade the video on my two old TURBOchannel
workstations, a 3000-300X running DU 4.0E, and a dual-boot 3000-700
running the VMS 7.2 Hobbyist release and the Tru64 5.1 Non-Commercial
kit.  I had a variety of TC frame buffers lying around, and while I
had the machines apart, I went ahead and did some compatibility tests
for posterity's sake.  Perhaps this information will be of use to the
many folks now buying discounted 3000 systems for hobbyist use.

None of the systems have Open3D installed, so these results reflect
only 2D compatibility.

Frame Buffer       Planes    DU 4.0E   Tru64 5.1   OpenVMS 7.2

300 internal (HX)     8        yes        yes*        yes*
PMAGB-B  (HX)         8        yes*       yes         yes
PMAG-E   (PXG)       24        no         no          no*
PMAG-J   (TX)         8        yes*       yes         no
PMAGD-AA (ZLX-E1)     8        yes*       yes         yes
PMAGD-BA (ZLX-E2)    24        yes*       yes         yes
PMAGD-CA (ZLX-E3)    24        yes        yes         yes

* configuration not tested here; entry based on other reports

For what it's worth, I believe that the 24-plane PMAGB-J would have
the same compatibility characteristics as the 8-plane PMAG-J listed
above.  This might be a cheap route to TrueColor for DU/T64 systems.

All of these cards, save the PMAG-E (and the 300's internal video),
occupy a single TURBOchannel slot.  The PMAG-E occupies two slots.

The best choices among the devices tested, in terms of color depth
and compatibility, are clearly the ZLX-E2 and ZLX-E3.  I ended up
leaving these in my own systems.

A warning:  if you're thinking about buying the Tru64 Non-Commercial
kit for your 3000, go ahead and do it soon.  Rumor has it that the
TURBOchannel drivers will be removed from 5.1A, so you'll want to
get the current 5.1 kit.


